=== meta ===
rule: ASSERT_WEAKENED
issue: 471
title: a setup call in a fixture's body is not its producer and lends no evidence
origin: ruling 471 Q1 (c), the analysis's Q1 cheat: the fixture calls init_db() and returns Ledger(),
origin2: and the diff keeps a no-op edit in init_db only. Only the producer, Ledger, counts, and it did
origin3: not change, so the weakened assertion blocks. Under Q1 (b) every call in the fixture's body would
origin4: have counted. An honest change in a setup call is the stated residual of the same rule.
=== before: app/db.py ===
def init_db():
    return []
=== after: app/db.py ===
def init_db():
    return [] + []
=== before: tests/test_billing.py ===
def test_total(ledger):
    assert ledger.total([50.0, 50.0]) == 100.0
=== after: tests/test_billing.py ===
def test_total(ledger):
    assert ledger.total([50.0, 50.0]) > 0
=== head: app/ledger.py ===
class Ledger:
    def total(self, items):
        return sum(items)
=== head: tests/conftest.py ===
